r decades in some form.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/04/california-resources-crc-q3-2019-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRC 2019 Q4","e":"crc","d":"2020-02-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Todd Stevens","x":"By consolidating and streamlining our operations teams in our core Bakersfield and Long Beach offices, we've been able to increase efficiency, reduce our staffing and improve margins.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/27/california-resources-crc-q4-2019-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRC 2019 Q4","e":"crc","d":"2020-02-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Smith","x":"We anticipate ongoing cost savings of approximately $50 million annually as a result of these organizational and operational improvements with slightly more than 50% of the reduction in G&A expenses and the remainder in production costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/27/california-resources-crc-q4-2019-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRC 2021 Q1","e":"crc","d":"2021-05-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Francisco J. Leon","x":"As a result, our first quarter 2021 G&A cost averaged $5.36 per BOE, which is $0.87 below the previous quarter, primarily due to our ongoing cost saving efforts and workforce reductions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/13/california-resources-corp-crc-q1-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRC 2021 Q1","e":"crc","d":"2021-05-13","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Francisco J. Leon","x":"Given our current performance, we are reaffirming guidance and expect to trend toward the high end of our free cash flow range, implying a free cash flow yield in the high teens, while assuming our current market capitalization.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/13/california-resources-corp-crc-q1-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRC 2021 Q2","e":"crc","d":"2021-08-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joanna Park","x":"The team continued to deliver on both aspects, maintaining corporate G&A cost savings, which are down 16% from 2020 levels and our controllable nonenergy costs, which are in line with the first quarter of 2021, both on a per barrel basis.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/06/california-resources-corp-crc-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRC 2021 Q2","e":"crc","d":"2021-08-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Joanna Park","x":"But from a high-level perspective, these bolt-on and bolt-off transactions allow us to recycle capital back into our core fields, simplify our business model and continue to streamline our cost structure.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/06/california-resources-corp-crc-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRC 2021 Q2","e":"crc","d":"2021-08-05","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Joanna Park","x":"…combined with our updated forecast, our free cash flow for the balance of the year, give us confidence to increase the full year guidance to the range of $400 million to $500 million and to increase our share repurchase program, as I mentioned earlier, by $100 million to $250 million in total.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/06/california-resources-corp-crc-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRC 2021 Q3","e":"crc","d":"2021-11-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Francisco J. Leon","x":"The combination of our strong operating results and streamlining of our asset portfolio continues to enhance our financial strength.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/11/california-resources-corp-crc-q3-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRC 2025 Q4","e":"crc","d":"2026-03-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Clio Crespy","x":"Yes, on synergy and our cost reduction journey, if you look at that graph that we shared with you all, since 2023 we have delivered $300,000,000 of structural cost reductions, and those are primarily driven by ERA integration—that was around $235,000,000.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/03/02/california-resources-crc-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"CRC 2026 Q1","e":"crc","d":"2026-05-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Clio Crespy","x":"Our cumulative synergy and structural cost reduction target through 2028 now stands at upwards of $460 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/crc-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRC 2026 Q1","e":"crc","d":"2026-05-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Clio Crespy","x":"So we laid out last quarter that we had already delivered roughly $300 million of structural cost reduction and that ahead of schedule.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/crc-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRC 2026 Q1","e":"crc","d":"2026-05-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Clio Crespy","x":"We delivered a strong first quarter with adjusted EBITDAX of $304 million, approximately 17% above the midpoint of our guidance, and we are raising our full year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/crc-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRC 2026 Q1","e":"crc","d":"2026-05-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Clio Crespy","x":"For the full year, we are raising our outlook across the board.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/crc-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRC 2026 Q2","e":"crc","d":"2026-08-10","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Francisco J. Leon","x":"Now you couple that with the Middle East conflict and it is leading to some near term conditions that are favoring refiners and on top of that, we are dealing with a pipeline operator that is behaving in a matter that we feel is inconsistent with established tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/17/crc-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRC 2026 Q2","e":"crc","d":"2026-08-10","l":"pricing_power","r":"managem